# CITATION file of AudioSet-Tools v2. Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# `date-released` is left out on purpose: it is set (together with the software DOI, once minted) when v2.0.0 is released.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AudioSet-Tools"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article (preferred citation); for the v2 architecture also cite the EUSIPCO 2026 poster, and for the data the AudioSet-EV records listed under references."
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - family-names: Giacomelli
    given-names: Stefano
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0438-1748"
    email: "stefano.giacomelli@graduate.univaq.it"
    affiliation: "University of L'Aquila, Department of Information Engineering, Computer Science and Mathematics (DISIM)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/StefanoGiacomelli/audioset-tools"
url: "https://github.com/StefanoGiacomelli/audioset-tools"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for taxonomy-aware curation of AudioSet, AudioSet Strong and VGGSound metadata: the sources are parsed
  into one normalized record model (AudioRecord, TemporalEvent, AudioDataset) with label-aware filtering in the id,
  original, SALT and auto query spaces, deterministic rebalancing, merging, statistics, lossless JSON/CSV export, event
  tracks and piano rolls, and an optional YouTube clip downloader with structured reports. The article cited below
  describes version 1 of the framework; version 2 is the standalone package presented in the EUSIPCO 2026 poster listed
  under references. Research activities were mainly funded under the Ministerial Decree (DM) 118/2023, Mission 4,
  Component 1, Investment 4.1 of the National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR) - "PNRR Research" - CUP:
  E11I23000100001. Research activities and publications were also partially supported by the European Union under the
  Italian National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR) of NextGenerationEU, within the partnership on
  "Telecommunications of the Future" (PE00000001 - RESTART), and by the European Union - NextGenerationEU under the
  Italian Ministry of University and Research (MUR), National Innovation Ecosystem grant ECS00000041 - VITALITY, CUP:
  E13C22001060006 (the funding statement of the article).
keywords:
  - AudioSet
  - AudioSet Strong
  - VGGSound
  - SALT
  - audio dataset curation
  - taxonomy
  - reproducible research
